WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:10.370
Hegan Reserve was an exercise in turning an
overgrown cow paddock into a place where visitors

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.730
could rest and relax.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:19.440
The natural environment would be restored,
native plants would line the stream and birds

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.560
and fish would return.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:27.940
The pupils of the neighbouring schools, Southbrook
Primary and Rangiora New Life, would use it

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:32.400
for learning, sporting events and recreation.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.720
Hegan Reserve is a resource that fits beautifully with our school's three kete:

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.440
knowledge, character and relationship.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.980
We use it to develop knowledge of our environment and the social sciences,

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.780
the sciences and our P.E. activities.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.160
It allows us the space to chill,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.600
giving children the chance to be outside to meditate,

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.580
to be creative in their thinking.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.980
It is a place to work for the community,

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.920
to be part of team activities

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.560
and to observe our native environment, all building relationships.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.920
Southbrook School is proud to be part of the Hegan Reserve.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:19.040
The seating was paid for by the Community Board,
as was year 13 student Joel Harnett’s sculpture

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:24.180
Middle Brook, which symbolises the character
of the stream as it winds its way through

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.680
the newly formed reserve.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:35.040
The poem, Hegan Reserve, installed at the
entrance was written by Southbrook pupil Jasmine Chivers

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.819
and speaks of her vision for the future
of the reserve:

00:01:38.819 --> 00:01:40.939
Kids are laughing
Dogs are barking

00:01:40.939 --> 00:01:43.259
Sounds of joy fill the air

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.060
The creek is babbling,
scorching feet paddling

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.900
toes tickling in the soft green grass

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.380
Through the planning and efforts of pupils

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.760
at Southbrook Primary School and Rangiora
New Life School and guidance from the Council’s

00:01:54.760 --> 00:02:01.960
Green Corps and Rangiora Community Board,
amazing progress has been made so far.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:07.060
Hegan Reserve the place to be, for picnics, hammocks, friends and family.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.860
Our board looks forward to continuing to work
with the schools and the wider community in

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:18.500
making Hegan Reserve an enviromental treasure
for generations to come.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.100
We love Hegan Reserve!

